# Production build values. Committed on purpose.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined into the client bundle at BUILD time, so it has to be
# present when the build runs — setting it as a Worker runtime variable does
# nothing, the bundle is already compiled by then. Cloudflare Workers Builds
# runs `opennextjs-cloudflare build` on its own runners, where neither
# .env.local nor the `convex deploy --cmd` wrapper in `pnpm deploy` exists, so
# without this file the production build compiles with no deployment URL and the
# app silently falls back to local-only mode.
#
# Keeping it here rather than in the Cloudflare dashboard means the value is
# reviewable, versioned, and cannot drift out of sync with the deployment.
#
# This is not a secret: the URL ships inside the client bundle either way, and
# access is gated by the identity checks inside each Convex function, never by
# the URL being unknown. The actual secret (ENCRYPTION_MASTER_KEY) stays a
# Cloudflare Worker secret and is never committed.
#
# .env.local wins over this file, so local builds keep pointing at the dev
# deployment; only builds without a .env.local (i.e. CI/Cloudflare) use it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL=https://befitting-badger-749.convex.cloud
